<title>LITHUANIA: ROKISHKIS DECIDES ON DIVIDENDS.</title>
<headline>ROKISHKIS DECIDES ON DIVIDENDS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rokishkis Cheese will pay dividends amounting to ten percent of the nominal value of its ordinary shares and one percent of the nominal value of its preferential shares, the Vilnius bourse said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The bourse said that Rokishkis made the decision at its general shareholders meeting last Friday.</p>
<p>The stock exchange also said that the company's shareholders failed to reach any agreement regarding the increase of share capital.</p>
<p>Rokishkis is one of Lithuania's leading blue chip stocks. Williams de Broe earlier this year bought a 14 percent stake in the company.</p>
<p>--Ed Stoddard, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
